& [CoreConclusion] is an LLM-assisted semantic compiler front end over human-authoritative SOP
  + SOP files should optimize articulated meaning, provenance, review, and coherent authorship rather than imitate neural storage layout
  + the compiler should emit normalized semantic identities and relations independently of source-file boundaries
  + Codex can scan bounded source and propose candidate concept boundaries, clauses, aliases, operations, relations, constraints, and unresolved ambiguities
  + a deterministic compiler and Observer review must decide structural validity, grounding, authority, commitment, and package admission
  + the exact semantic fabric compiles before vector, router, denoiser, graph-neural, or language-model artifacts
  + conventional model-building code projects training examples, trains or calibrates parameters, evaluates them, and binds the admitted artifact to exact fabric and corpus digests
  = concise: Codex proposes semantic IR; Cantor commits an exact fabric; a model builder derives the neural fabric

& [AuthoringCompilationDelineation] removes the false file-layout burden
  + [source_document] is a coherent human-readable authorship and review unit
  + [source_clause] is an exact addressable byte span within a preserved source version
  + [semantic_identity] is a stable concept or operation identity independent of file path and line number
  + [semantic_relation] is a separately typed and sourced edge between identities
  + [semantic_commit] is one atomic admitted transaction containing a primary identity revision and its required dependent records
  + [neural_projection] is a derived model-facing encoding over one or more semantic records
  = must: permit one document to declare many concepts and one concept to accumulate separately attributed clauses across documents
  = must: preserve every many-to-many source-to-semantic mapping
  - never: require one file per concept merely to obtain normalized storage
  - never: infer that one concept, graph node, embedding, output label, and physical neuron are the same object

& [MinimalCommittedEntry] is semantic atomicity rather than textual smallness
  + [primary_key] is stable SemanticAddress plus immutable revision identity
  + [kind] distinguishes identity, operation, relation, constraint, contract, purpose, context, evidence, faculty program, fault, or other declared form
  + [articulated_meaning] is the smallest meaning that can remain truthful and usable without omitted governing context
  + [scope_and_purpose] records where and why the meaning applies
  + [identity_boundary] records required invariants, exclusions, and permitted variation
  + [source_grounding] records exact package, document, span, quote, and digest evidence
  + [authority_and_lifecycle] records proposer, reviewer, signer scope, status, version, supersession, and revocation
  + [dependent_records] are labels, aliases, typed relations, operation roles, conditions, examples, counterexamples, unresolved alternatives, and proofs
  = must: commit the primary revision and all integrity-required dependent records atomically
  = must: keep optional projections independently rebuildable
  = must: define minimal by semantic and transactional sufficiency rather than byte count

& [CandidateSemanticIR] is the non-authoritative LLM output
  + [scan_job] binds model, prompt profile, source snapshot set, exact bytes, tool version, budget, and random or deterministic settings
  + [candidate_identity] carries proposed kind, stable-key suggestion, preferred label, aliases, meaning, scope, purpose, and confidence
  + [candidate_clause] carries normalized proposition, modality, conditions, exceptions, and exact source spans
  + [candidate_relation] carries source identity, target identity or unresolved reference, relation type, direction, context, and supporting spans
  + [candidate_operation] carries verb identity, role signature, preconditions, invariants, outputs, failures, effects, and supporting spans
  + [candidate_boundary] carries invariants, exclusions, ambiguity, collision, and suspected cross-identity merge or split
  + [candidate_unresolved] preserves alternative parses, missing anchors, contradictions, inferred-but-undeclared relations, and questions
  + [candidate_provenance] carries model and request identity, extraction explanation, span evidence, confidence, and all transformations
  = must: represent absence, uncertainty, disagreement, and alternatives explicitly
  = must: distinguish quoted declaration, normalized restatement, and model inference
  - never: acquire authority merely because a schema validates or confidence is high

& [CompilationPipeline] is staged and replayable
  * freeze and hash an immutable SOP source snapshot
  * parse all supported explicit forms through the existing deterministic parser
  * ask Codex to scan the same bounded bytes and emit schema-valid CandidateSemanticIR only
  * reconcile parser facts with model candidates while preserving additions, conflicts, merges, splits, omissions, and alternatives
  * apply Honesty grounding, Security authority and boundary, Refiner minimality, Scribe source-preservation, Weaver relation, Planner dependency, and Observer disposition reviews
  * commit accepted MinimalCommittedEntry transactions into the exact SemanticFabric
  * compile signed hash, relational, graph, lexical, provenance, source-map, quote, and optional vector indexes
  * project exact records and reviewed decisions into versioned corpus examples
  * train or calibrate an optional router, denoiser, graph model, or semantic transition model
  * evaluate against deterministic and equal-budget baselines, bind all fabric and corpus digests, sign, admit, and retain fallback
  = must: let every later stage be regenerated from admitted earlier artifacts
  = must: fail closed rather than convert an unsupported candidate into an implicit declaration

& [LLMCompilerAssistantRole] assigns interpretation without authority
  + [good_at] is recognizing paraphrase, cross-clause context, implicit candidate boundaries, aliases, conceptual duplicates, possible relationships, examples, and ambiguities
  + [good_at] is proposing a more coherent normalized expression while preserving the original quote and transformation trace
  + [not_authority_for] is source truth, semantic identity, signer scope, authorization, contract satisfaction, model training admission, or package signing
  + [not_authority_for] is silently filling an omitted premise, choosing among unresolved meanings, or merging identities because they are similar
  + [review_relation] is advisory Scribe plus Refiner proposal reviewed by all materially pertinent faculties
  = must: label every unsupported semantic addition as inference rather than source declaration
  = must: preserve model disagreement as useful review and training evidence

& [NeuralNodeDelineation] preserves inspectability without claiming localist neurons
  + [semantic_graph_node] may map one-to-one to an admitted SemanticAddress when useful
  + [embedding_record] may map one admitted address to one versioned vector while remaining only a retrieval projection
  + [model_output_class] may use SemanticAddress identifiers so predictions resolve to inspectable records
  + [graph_neural_state] may compute per-node activations while learned transformation weights are shared and distributed
  + [routing_region] may coarsen several semantic identities under an explicit correspondence and loss record
  + [physical_neuron_or_parameter] normally participates distributively and does not carry one authoritative concept
  = conclusion: design explicit semantic nodes fully; train neural parameters as subordinate distributed routing state

& [NeuralFabricBlueprint] is the compact LLM-proposed model specification
  + [target_profile] fixes supported layer families, tensor ranks, dimensions, activations, normalization, sparsity, quantization, and runtime constraints
  + [semantic_topology] maps exact SemanticAddresses and typed relations into nodes, hyperedges, channels, neighborhoods, and permitted message routes
  + [module_allocation] assigns identity, operation, boundary, provenance, temporal, attention, faculty, and abstention functions to declared modules
  + [node_initialization] proposes address-bound prototypes, feature sources, initialization class, scale, and confidence
  + [edge_initialization] proposes relation-conditioned transforms, direction, gate prior, inhibition or excitation role, and supporting semantics
  + [hard_masks] compile exact impossibility, authority, lifecycle, and effect boundaries that learning cannot override
  + [soft_priors] initialize traversal, attention, uncertainty, cost, and route preferences without becoming semantic truth
  + [output_mapping] resolves every output position to a SemanticAddress, operation, fault, abstention, or declared auxiliary signal
  + [loss_and_curriculum] proposes reviewed examples, negative cases, faculty checks, and staged objectives without authorizing training
  + [correspondence_manifest] records exact, coarsened, omitted, synthesized, shared, and learned portions of the model
  = must: remain compact enough for human inspection, deterministic validation, hashing, diff, and replay
  = must: bind every semantically named element to admitted exact fabric records
  - never: accept arbitrary executable model code or unbounded tensor payload as a blueprint

& [ShapeDelineation] separates semantic topology from compute architecture
  + [semantic_shape] is the corpus-specific typed graph, hypergraph, namespaces, boundaries, routes, and sparse activation regions
  + [compute_shape] is the layer and tensor architecture that processes the semantic shape
  + [selected_first_policy] fixes a small relation-aware sparse router architecture while allowing the compiled semantic topology and masks to vary by admitted fabric
  + [later_policy] may let a constrained generator select among proved module templates or propose bounded architecture deltas
  = must: measure fixed-architecture semantic preloading before neural architecture generation
  - never: let architectural novelty obscure whether semantic initialization itself caused the gain

& [WeightPreloadClasses] moves from safest and most inspectable to most learned
  + [class_0_exact] is deterministic adjacency, typed masks, lookup identity, source coverage, authority exclusions, and output-address mapping
  + [class_1_semantic] is definition-derived node embeddings, relation prototypes, faculty labels, and declared contextual scores
  + [class_2_LLM_proposed] is bounded gate priors, module assignments, prototype mixtures, low-rank factors, and curriculum proposals with explanations
  + [class_3_calibrated] is optimizer-adjusted parameters learned from reviewed training and validation examples
  + [class_4_generated] is raw tensor blocks emitted by a task-trained hypernetwork or weight-generation model
  = must: preserve the originating class for every parameter or parameter block
  = must: compare each added class against the immediately simpler initialization
  = conclusion: the LLM can preload meaningful structured state immediately; direct full-weight generation is a later learned capability

& [DeterministicTensorBuilder] materializes a blueprint without interpreting meaning
  + [input] is one admitted SemanticFabric, one validated NeuralFabricBlueprint, one target profile, and frozen build settings
  + [validation] checks identities, relations, dimensions, numerical ranges, masks, coverage, sparsity, unsupported modules, and all digests
  + [materialization] allocates topology, embeddings, transforms, biases, masks, output heads, metadata, and initialization-class ledger
  + [normalization] applies declared deterministic scaling, seeding, orthogonalization, clipping, and quantization policies
  + [output] is an unsigned candidate model artifact plus exact build and correspondence manifests
  + [admission] occurs only after calibration, held-out evaluation, fault tests, and signatures
  = must: produce byte-replayable tensors under a deterministic target profile where supported
  - never: repair an invalid LLM blueprint by silently inventing dimensions, mappings, or weights

& [GenericLLMVersusWeightGenerator] preserves the feasible boundary
  + [general_Codex] can reason about semantic topology, select constrained templates, produce structured priors, and explain mappings
  + [general_Codex_limit] has no direct task-loss feedback, tensor-native output channel, or guarantee that guessed raw floating-point blocks form a good model
  + [trained_hypernetwork] learns a function from task or fabric conditions to another network's weights
  + [diffusion_weight_generator] learns distributions over useful parameter blocks from trained-model checkpoints
  + [Cantor_progression] uses Codex blueprint generation first and trains a dedicated Cantor weight generator only after many reviewed fabric-to-model outcomes exist
  = conclusion: a model can generate another model's weights, but expertise must be demonstrated for the exact Cantor target and workload

& [ResearchCorrespondence] establishes precedent without claiming Cantor proof
  + [HyperNetworks_2016] demonstrates a learned network generating weights for another network
  + [GNN2GNN_2022] demonstrates learned proposal of neural architecture represented through graphs
  + [D2NWG_2024] investigates diffusion-based generation of neural-network weights conditioned on target data
  + [DenoisedNeuralWeights_2024] investigates text-conditioned diffusion generation of initialization weights for new concepts
  + [Cantor_delta] is compile signed semantic fabric into an inspectable blueprint and evaluate semantic initialization under proof and authority constraints
  + [HyperNetworks_source] is https://arxiv.org/abs/1609.09106
  + [GNN2GNN_source] is https://proceedings.mlr.press/v180/agiollo22a.html
  + [D2NWG_source] is https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.18153
  + [DenoisedNeuralWeights_source] is https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.11966
  = must: treat these as feasibility precedents rather than evidence that Cantor's proposed initialization is effective

& [WeightPreloadAblation] is the required proof
  + [A] is fixed architecture with standard random initialization and exact masks only
  + [B] is A plus deterministic definition embeddings and relation prototypes
  + [C] is B plus Codex-proposed gate priors, module assignment, and low-rank seeds
  + [D] is C plus ordinary calibration or training on the same reviewed corpus
  + [E] is a later dedicated weight generator under the same target, data, and compute budget
  + [metrics] are route accuracy, recall, abstention, calibration, proof coverage, forbidden-route rate, convergence steps, final quality, latency, memory, and artifact size
  + [causal_claim] C improves preloading only when it exceeds B across held-out fabrics and repeated seeds
  + [expert_claim] remains absent until the improvement is robust, reproducible, and materially useful

& [ToolBoundary] uses the existing Codex seam without conflating analysis and commitment
  + [current_surface] query_sop is already a proven read-only MCP projection of Cantor exact query behavior
  + [candidate_read_tool] is propose_semantic_ir over one exact snapshot or bounded batch, returning CandidateSemanticIR without repository or authority mutation
  + [future_write_tool] is submit_semantic_candidate or commit_semantic_revision and remains separate, approval-bearing, review-gated, and unauthorized by this assessment
  + [batch_controller] may use the Codex SDK to start, continue, resume, budget, and archive bounded scan jobs
  + [deep_client] may use Codex App Server only when a custom interactive product needs streamed thread, event, approval, and history integration
  + [tool_description] declares purpose, precise schema, stable identifiers, side effects, authority absence, limits, and failure behavior
  = must: keep read/proposal and write/commit capabilities separate
  = must: use MCP as the first natural live tool-and-context boundary for Codex
  + [official_tool_design] is https://developers.openai.com/plugins/plan/tools
  + [official_MCP] is https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/extend/mcp
  + [official_Codex_SDK] is https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/codex-sdk
  + [official_App_Server] is https://learn.chatgpt.com/docs/app-server

& [ThreeBuildMeanings] prevents the word compile from hiding incompatible work
  + [index_build] creates exact indexes, embeddings, or approximate-nearest-neighbor structures without training a language model
  + [model_training] optimizes router, denoiser, graph, or transition-model parameters from reviewed examples
  + [runtime_packaging] converts an evaluated model and metadata into a provider artifact such as a llama.cpp-compatible runtime package
  = must: select, version, test, and authorize each stage independently

& [FirstExperiment] is candidate extraction over a fixed signed corpus
  + [corpus] is a small package of existing signed SOP sources with exact parser results and human-reviewable meanings
  + [runs] are two independent Codex scans plus one deterministic parser baseline under frozen profiles
  + [output] is CandidateSemanticIR JSON only with no repository mutation or semantic admission
  + [review] compares proposed identities, clauses, relations, operations, boundaries, and unresolved alternatives
  + [adjudication] is an attributed Observer review producing accept, refine, split, merge, reject, or unresolved dispositions
  + [result] is one exact test SemanticFabric plus a preserved negative and disagreement corpus
  + [stop] occurs before embedding or model training unless extraction and commitment gates pass

& [EvaluationSet] measures semantic digestion rather than fluency
  + [concept_recall_and_precision] compare reviewed necessary identities with proposed identities
  + [unsupported_identity_rate] measures nodes without sufficient source grounding
  + [unsupported_relation_rate] measures edges stated as declarations without sufficient source grounding
  + [span_exactness] measures correct byte and clause evidence
  + [merge_error] measures distinct meanings collapsed into one identity
  + [split_error] measures one identity fragmented without semantic cause
  + [duplicate_rate] measures redundant identities and relations
  + [ambiguity_preservation] measures unresolved alternatives retained rather than guessed away
  + [proof_completeness] measures model, source, transformation, disposition, and package lineage
  + [reproducibility] measures normalized candidate agreement across repeated runs
  + [work] is tokens, bytes, latency, cost, reviewer time, and deterministic compiler time

& [FaultSet] is mandatory
  + [source_fabric_collapse] makes optimized storage shape dictate human meaning
  + [file_identity_collapse] treats path or line as stable semantic identity
  + [semantic_neuron_collapse] treats a concept as one physical neuron or learned weight
  + [model_authority_laundering] converts an LLM proposal into signed truth without review
  + [implicit_relation_laundering] stores plausible inferred edges as declared source meaning
  + [provenance_loss] normalizes a concept without exact reversible source grounding
  + [over_atomization] removes context required for truthful meaning
  + [under_atomization] commits several separable identities as one unstable record
  + [cross_version_mix] combines source, candidates, corpus, exact fabric, and neural artifacts from different digests
  + [self_training_loop] retrains on model-generated interpretations without reviewed outcomes
  + [unmeasured_neuralization] adds learned complexity before exact baselines and measurable gain

& [CandidateRequirementSet] is CSAC-001 through CSAC-034
  + [CSAC-001] keep SOP documents human-authoritative and coherent rather than shaped as neural storage
  + [CSAC-002] map source documents and clauses many-to-many with stable semantic identities
  + [CSAC-003] define MinimalCommittedEntry as an atomic semantically sufficient transaction
  + [CSAC-004] separate primary identity records from normalized dependent labels, relations, operations, boundaries, and proof
  + [CSAC-005] define CandidateSemanticIR as non-authoritative model output
  + [CSAC-006] bind every scan to exact source, model, prompt, tool, settings, and budget identities
  + [CSAC-007] distinguish source declaration, normalized restatement, and model inference
  + [CSAC-008] preserve ambiguity, alternatives, omissions, contradiction, and disagreement
  + [CSAC-009] compare LLM extraction with deterministic parser evidence
  + [CSAC-010] review candidates through materially pertinent faculty programs and Observer disposition
  + [CSAC-011] commit only reviewed identities and dependent records into the authoritative exact fabric
  + [CSAC-012] compile exact graph, relational, hash, lexical, provenance, source, quote, and optional vector projections first
  + [CSAC-013] derive reviewed corpus examples only from version-bound exact and disposition records
  + [CSAC-014] keep learned artifacts replaceable, subordinate, coverage-declared, and deterministically gated
  + [CSAC-015] bind every admitted neural artifact to exact fabric, corpus, compiler, training, and evaluation digests
  + [CSAC-016] distinguish semantic graph nodes, embedding records, model labels, routing regions, and physical learned parameters
  + [CSAC-017] forbid authoritative meaning from residing only in distributed neural parameters
  + [CSAC-018] expose proposal analysis separately from commit or mutation authority
  + [CSAC-019] prefer a bounded MCP proposal tool for live Codex use
  + [CSAC-020] use the Codex SDK only when an external batch controller is required
  + [CSAC-021] define explicit tool schemas, limits, side effects, failure behavior, and stable IDs
  + [CSAC-022] evaluate concept, relation, source-span, ambiguity, proof, reproducibility, and work metrics
  + [CSAC-023] require independent scans, deterministic baseline, and attributed adjudication in the first experiment
  + [CSAC-024] stop before training until extraction, commitment, corpus, baseline, and neural adoption gates pass
  + [CSAC-025] distinguish index construction, model training, and runtime packaging
  + [CSAC-026] preserve deterministic correctness and query fallback when the LLM or neural artifact is absent
  + [CSAC-027] define one constrained NeuralFabricBlueprint with exact semantic correspondence
  + [CSAC-028] separate fabric-specific semantic topology from reusable compute architecture
  + [CSAC-029] preload exact masks, address mappings, embeddings, relation prototypes, gate priors, and bounded low-rank seeds by declared class
  + [CSAC-030] validate and materialize every blueprint through a deterministic target-profile builder
  + [CSAC-031] forbid silent tensor repair and unbounded raw-weight payloads from a general LLM
  + [CSAC-032] distinguish general LLM blueprint proposal from a task-trained hypernetwork or diffusion weight generator
  + [CSAC-033] compare random, deterministic-semantic, LLM-proposed, calibrated, and generated-weight initialization under one ablation
  + [CSAC-034] require held-out, repeated, causal evidence before calling the preload expert or admitting it

& [Decision] is preserve and fully process the compiler-assistant candidate before implementation
  + [canonical_authority] existing semantic IR, trusted compilation, self-hosting, exact query, neural boundary, database, and MCP specifications remain authoritative within their scopes
  + [new_canonical_authority] is absent
  + [new_implementation_authority] is absent
  + [model_training_authority] is absent
  + [schedule_effect] add CSAC-SJS-01 after WPIO data-form reconciliation and before CSDL neural-model implementation
  + [first_implementation_candidate] after full SJS is one schema-bound proposal-only scan over a fixed signed corpus followed by an offline blueprint-and-initialization ablation if extraction gates pass
  + [reasoning_depth] current compiler and identity reconciliation requires deeper architecture reasoning; a frozen-schema extraction harness becomes Spark-suitable after signed activation authority exists
